      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fair point, but we already have the same issue for other configs:\n\n* label and submit requirement definitions in child projects are ignored if the parent disallows overriding them\n* permissions in child projects are ignored if they are blocked in a parent project\n* the code-owners plugin already has FORCED as value for some of its congifs\n\nSo while this is not perfect, it\u0027s consistent with what we already have.\nI added a note about this to the commit message.\n\nTo mitigate the concern I added debug logs, so that onduty can find that there are configured defaults by doing a trace.\n\nHaving looked at the code-owners plugin I notified that we use \u0027FORCED\u0027 there, so for consistency I changed \u0027ENFORCED\u0027 to \u0027FORCED\u0027 here.",
